# SQL's `like` with a prefix pattern: DS0105 suggesting `startswith`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where customerId like 'c-%'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..48
  PIPELINE@0..47
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..47
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..47
        NAME_REF@26..36
          IDENT@26..36 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
        IDENT@37..41 "like"
        WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
        LITERAL@42..47
          STRING@42..47 "'c-%'"
  WHITESPACE@47..48 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `like` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where customerId like 'c-%'
  |                                      ^^^^ this is SQL's pattern match
  |
  = help: use `startswith`: `customerId startswith 'c-'`
  = note: `startswith` ignores case; `startswith_cs` matches case exactly
